// /learn/frameql-an-introduction — hosts the deposited **v2.3** source (2026-08-23), byte-identical to
// the Zenodo record: sha256 ea52d43a…6d6327, 28,310 bytes, verified against
// zenodo.org/api/records/22071910 by downloading the deposit's own .md and comparing, not against the
// filename. Title/subtitle come from the deposit's own front-matter; the DOI and edition line below
// are page CHROME, so nothing is injected into the hosted markdown. Middle rung of the FrameQL
// ladder: /learn/frameql-primer (8 min) → this introduction (25 min) → the Manual (/docs/frameql).
//
// RE-EDITIONED v2.1 → v2.3 (Huayin's ruling, 2026-08-23, Unit 2). Same shape as this file's two
// earlier swaps — v1 → v1.1 (f27318d) and v1.1 → v2.1 (2026-08-23) — and for the same reason: this
// route is a byte-faithful deposited-edition surface, so the move is a REPOINT and never an edit.
// Same URL, new edition, superseded editions retained on disk and unimported exactly as
// `frameql_an_introduction_v1_1.md`, `launch_story_v6` and the 6e/6f manual editions are.
//
// IT SKIPS v2.2 ON PURPOSE. `w-frameql-introduction.r06` (v2.2, 22071508) is a real deposit and a
// first-class record; it was current for part of one day and superseded by v2.3 the same day. A route
// renders the edition that is CURRENT, not every edition that existed, so v2.2 is never hosted here.
// The registry is where its life is recorded.
//
// WHAT THE NEW EDITION CHANGES: v2.3 advances the theory reference to The Theory of Data v6.1
// (10.5281/zenodo.22013410), cites the Manual's compatibility statement as the normative seam for
// retained implementation vocabulary, and updates companion references. Shipped Frame-QL syntax and
// behaviour are unchanged. The Manual remains normative for shipped syntax and behaviour; this route
// is the conceptual on-ramp, not the reference.
//
// The ```frameql fences fall back to plaintext under the site's Shiki (no highlighter error). The
// deposit's LaTeX — eleven `$$…$$` blocks and the inline `$F@A$` — renders through the site's math
// pipeline (astro.config.mjs, PR #212); none of it required touching these frozen bytes.
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Content, frontmatter } from '../../content/corpus/frameql_an_introduction_v2_3.md';
const DOI = '10.5281/zenodo.22071910';
const EDITION = 'Version 2.3 · 23 August 2026';
---
<BaseLayout title="Frame-QL: An Introduction — datumwise"
  description="The introduction to Frame-QL — the output frame is the query. Why rows, tables, joins, and GROUP BY are not primitives of the request interface, and where AI belongs at the intent boundary.">
  <div class="page-head">
    <p class="kicker"><a href="/learn">Learn</a></p>
    <h1 class="serif">{frontmatter.title}</h1>
    <p class="lede">{frontmatter.subtitle}</p>
    <p class="doi mono">{EDITION} · <a href={`https://doi.org/${DOI}`} rel="noopener" target="_blank">doi.org/{DOI}</a></p>
  </div>

  <article class="prose">
    <Content />
  </article>

  <p class="evidence-note">
    <strong>This edition.</strong> The page above is <em>Frame-QL: An Introduction</em>,
    <strong>Version 2.3</strong>, deposited <strong>23 August 2026</strong>, reproduced from the
    deposit byte for byte. It supersedes the Version 2.1 edition previously served at this URL, whose
    record — like every earlier one, including the Version 2.2 edition this URL never served —
    remains in the publication registry. The Frame-QL Manual stays authoritative for shipped syntax
    and behaviour; this is the conceptual on-ramp, not the reference.
  </p>

  <p class="engage wayfinding">
    Shorter first: <a href="/learn/frameql-primer">A Primer on Frame-QL</a> ·
    Lighter still: <a href="/what-is-frameql">What is FrameQL — and why?</a> ·
    The reference, complete: <a href="/docs/frameql">the FrameQL Manual</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-head { width: min(100% - 3rem, var(--measure)); margin: 0 auto; }
  .page-head h1 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4vw, 2.6rem); margin: 0.3rem 0 0.5rem; }
  .kicker a { color: var(--ink-faint); text-decoration: none; }
  .kicker a:hover { color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .lede { font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .doi { font-size: 0.8rem; margin-top: 0.4rem; }
  .doi a { color: var(--ink-faint); }
  .evidence-note { width: min(100% - 3rem, var(--measure)); margin: 3rem auto 0; padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .engage { width: min(100% - 3rem, var(--measure)); margin: 1.5rem auto 0;
    font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
</style>
